WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:22.080
Look over there.

00:22.080 --> 00:52.040
So that's what's been happening to our capital.

00:52.080 --> 00:57.080
It is as I promised, O Winnermucca.

00:57.080 --> 00:59.080
The cattle are in the small canyon.

00:59.080 --> 01:00.080
Your people are grateful.

01:00.080 --> 01:02.080
Take them quickly, if the Cartwrights come.

01:02.080 --> 01:07.080
The Cartwrights are here.

01:07.080 --> 01:11.080
You know what happens to cattle thieves?

01:11.080 --> 01:40.080
Shoot, Ben Cartwright. Shoot!

01:40.080 --> 02:03.080
Look what I trusted you.

02:03.080 --> 02:05.080
I gave you a good life in the Ponderosa.

02:05.080 --> 02:07.080
Do you repay me by stealing my cattle?

02:07.080 --> 02:10.080
Do not blame my brother.

02:10.080 --> 02:12.080
He but did the word of his chief.

02:12.080 --> 02:14.080
How long have the Paiutes been cattle thieves?

02:14.080 --> 02:17.080
Since the Washoe Antelope and deer are gone.

02:17.080 --> 02:21.080
Since the pinion tree burns in the fires of Sun Mountain.

02:21.080 --> 02:27.080
Since our women and our children and our braves sit hungry in our tents and sick and without food.

02:27.080 --> 02:30.080
What say you, Winnermucca?

02:30.080 --> 02:34.080
The Washoe Antelope herds have fed the Paiutes since the long ago dream time.

02:34.080 --> 02:39.080
The diggers of Sun Mountain eat antelope while the pots of the Paiute are empty.

02:39.080 --> 02:41.080
They are but three head.

02:41.080 --> 02:43.080
The weakest of the Ponderosa herd.

02:43.080 --> 02:45.080
Tukwa cannot see his people starve.

02:45.080 --> 02:47.080
What's the matter with you, Tukwa?

02:47.080 --> 02:50.080
The Cartwrights let the Paiutes starve?

02:50.080 --> 02:51.080
Why didn't you ask us?

02:51.080 --> 02:53.080
The Paiute is a man.

02:53.080 --> 02:56.080
He does not beg.

02:56.080 --> 03:02.080
Even now, Winnermucca is called woman by my young men around the council fires.

03:02.080 --> 03:04.080
Winnermucca is no woman.

03:04.080 --> 03:06.080
He thinks of his people.

03:06.080 --> 03:09.080
The ways of peace are good ways.

03:09.080 --> 03:13.080
But because the Paiute loves peace does not mean he cannot make war.

03:13.080 --> 03:17.080
War brings nothing but wailing in tents and lodges, Winnermucca.

03:17.080 --> 03:20.080
For the Paiute and the white man, you and I understand these things.

03:20.080 --> 03:24.080
Does Ben Cartwright disregard the voices of his sons?

03:24.080 --> 03:28.080
Even so, Winnermucca hears the words of his young men.

03:28.080 --> 03:30.080
They speak for war.

03:30.080 --> 03:32.080
They see as I see.

03:32.080 --> 03:35.080
That the Paiute walks the same trail as the antelope.

03:35.080 --> 03:37.080
And the antelope is dead.

03:37.080 --> 03:41.080
The men who dig in the earth are new to Washowinemucca.

03:41.080 --> 03:44.080
They do not know the ways of the land.

03:44.080 --> 03:47.080
My sons and I, we will ride to them and make them understand.

03:47.080 --> 03:49.080
They will listen.

03:49.080 --> 03:53.080
The Cartwrights and the Paiutes have long walked the earth together.

03:53.080 --> 03:59.080
But if there is war, Ben Cartwright, even the men of the Ponderosa can die.

03:59.080 --> 04:01.080
There will be no war.

04:01.080 --> 04:04.080
And no more antelope will die.

04:04.080 --> 04:06.080
I will see to it.

04:07.080 --> 04:09.080
Tukwa always speaks the truth.

04:09.080 --> 04:12.080
They must indeed be the weakest cattle of our herd.

04:12.080 --> 04:16.080
For our friendship, would you drive them off the Ponderosa?

04:16.080 --> 04:25.080
Help your people, Tukwa.

04:38.080 --> 04:42.080
Paul, I don't like all that war talk.

04:42.080 --> 04:46.080
I knew Virginia City is full of fools.

04:46.080 --> 04:48.080
They gave in fools that know you can't push Indians around.

04:48.080 --> 04:50.080
All they were thinking about was food.

04:50.080 --> 04:53.080
Food is one thing, destroying the balance of nature is another.

04:53.080 --> 04:55.080
To keep this up, the whole of Washowinemucca will become a desert.

04:55.080 --> 04:57.080
Saw it happen at John Sutter's California.

04:57.080 --> 04:58.080
All right, let's go.

04:58.080 --> 04:59.080
Where, Paul?

04:59.080 --> 05:00.080
Virginia City.

05:00.080 --> 05:26.080
Hey Adam, you see that little gal smiling at me?

05:26.080 --> 05:29.080
What makes you think it's you she was smiling at?

05:29.080 --> 05:31.080
You know, every time I come in here, I gotta get used to it all over again.

05:31.080 --> 05:33.080
Remember when this was nothing more than a jack rabbit run?

05:33.080 --> 05:36.080
Yeah, I don't know what I like a jack rabbit better, little Joe.

05:36.080 --> 05:39.080
All right, you two country boys, get you filled with the city.

05:39.080 --> 05:41.080
Adam and I'll take a little look around.

05:41.080 --> 05:43.080
Let's go.

05:47.080 --> 05:50.080
Hey horse, you ever see anything like this in your whole life?

05:52.080 --> 05:56.080
Yeah, I seen a stampede last fall up in Silver Matter.

05:56.080 --> 05:59.080
Only difference, Paul, is the stampede made more sense.

05:59.080 --> 06:01.080
Come on before you take free.

06:08.080 --> 06:10.080
Looks good, Lord.

06:10.080 --> 06:12.080
I wish there was more.

06:14.080 --> 06:18.080
Guess we've seen it all now, the good and the bad.

06:18.080 --> 06:21.080
Is this what they call striking it rich?

06:21.080 --> 06:24.080
Looks like all they've struck so far is bad luck.

06:24.080 --> 06:27.080
Pretty rough on young ones like that.

06:34.080 --> 06:35.080
Howdy.

06:35.080 --> 06:37.080
Howdy.

06:37.080 --> 06:40.080
It's not much of a meal for grown boys.

06:41.080 --> 06:44.080
That ain't much of a meal for anybody, but that's my business, ain't it?

06:44.080 --> 06:48.080
No offense intended, Mr. Harris.

06:48.080 --> 06:51.080
Carl Harris is my wife and my boys.

06:51.080 --> 06:53.080
Hello, howdy.

06:53.080 --> 06:55.080
Howdy.

06:55.080 --> 06:58.080
You know, Mr. Harris, you could be feeding those boys beef.

06:59.080 --> 07:02.080
Yeah, if they had wings, they could fly too.

07:02.080 --> 07:05.080
Mr. Harris, we're the Cotrights from the Ponderosa.

07:05.080 --> 07:07.080
Now, there's plenty of beef in the valley.

07:07.080 --> 07:09.080
I reckon so.

07:09.080 --> 07:13.080
All I can do to fork over ten dollars a pound for that skinny antelope,

07:13.080 --> 07:15.080
I couldn't afford beef.

07:15.080 --> 07:16.080
Wait, ten dollars a pound?

07:16.080 --> 07:18.080
And lucky to get it.

07:18.080 --> 07:23.080
A man come through last week selling salt pork for fifteen dollars a pound.

07:24.080 --> 07:26.080
At least this meat is fresh.

07:26.080 --> 07:29.080
We aren't starving, mister. We take care of ourselves.

07:29.080 --> 07:31.080
Well, I'm sure you do, ma'am.

07:31.080 --> 07:32.080
You don't have to pay those prices.

07:32.080 --> 07:36.080
But we market our steers over to Placidville for twenty-five dollars a head.

07:36.080 --> 07:39.080
We'll be making money selling them to you for twenty.

07:40.080 --> 07:41.080
Twenty dollars?

07:41.080 --> 07:49.080
That's right.

07:49.080 --> 07:51.080
Are you joking me, mister?

07:51.080 --> 07:53.080
They're yours if you want them.

07:53.080 --> 08:00.080
All you have to do is come over to the Ponderosa and drive them away.

08:00.080 --> 08:04.080
Woo!

08:04.080 --> 08:08.080
I couldn't do much better than that back home in Kentucky.

08:08.080 --> 08:10.080
Kentucky? You're a long way from home.

08:10.080 --> 08:13.080
I got tired of seeing my family starve on forty acres of rock.

08:13.080 --> 08:17.080
Now I figured if we had to starve, we might as well do it somewhere with us a chance of striking it rich.

08:17.080 --> 08:19.080
Nobody's gonna starve, but we have catalysts there.

08:19.080 --> 08:21.080
Now get yourself some men together and come over to the Ponderosa.

08:21.080 --> 08:26.080
Well, by golly, we'll do it.

08:26.080 --> 08:28.080
Oh, do you hear that woman?

08:28.080 --> 08:30.080
We're gonna eat ourselves some beef.

08:30.080 --> 08:33.080
Oh, here I am acting like a Yankee.

08:33.080 --> 08:34.080
Come on in, have a cup of coffee.

08:34.080 --> 08:39.080
Mr. Harris, you sure don't know anything about us Yankees.

08:39.080 --> 08:41.080
You're a Yankee?

08:41.080 --> 08:42.080
Oh, I didn't mean it.

08:42.080 --> 08:43.080
Oh, it's all right, it's all right.

08:43.080 --> 08:45.080
Come on in, have some coffee.

08:45.080 --> 08:47.080
Howdy, howdy.

08:47.080 --> 08:49.080
Come on, butcher, let's go.

08:49.080 --> 08:51.080
Hurry up, let's go.

08:51.080 --> 08:53.080
Antelope meat, ten dollars a pound.

08:53.080 --> 08:57.080
Yeah, looks like we're raising our own kind of stock, don't we?

08:57.080 --> 08:59.080
Come on.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.080
Hurry up, let's go.

09:01.080 --> 09:03.080
Come on.

09:03.080 --> 09:06.080
Here, let me try a little, Joe.

09:06.080 --> 09:08.080
Excuse me, man.

09:08.080 --> 09:11.080
Excuse me.

09:11.080 --> 09:13.080
Excuse me.

09:13.080 --> 09:15.080
Excuse me.

09:15.080 --> 09:17.080
Give me some money, sir.

09:17.080 --> 09:19.080
Give me some money.

09:19.080 --> 09:21.080
Give me some money.

09:21.080 --> 09:23.080
Get back here.

09:23.080 --> 09:25.080
Get back here.

09:25.080 --> 09:27.080
Get back here.

09:27.080 --> 09:29.080
Hundred and a half, fifty dollars.

09:29.080 --> 09:32.080
They must be out of their minds.

09:32.080 --> 09:34.080
How so, friend?

09:34.080 --> 09:38.080
Always like to hear the other fellow's side of things.

09:38.080 --> 09:40.080
Ten dollars a pound for antelope meat.

09:40.080 --> 09:41.080
That makes sense to you?

09:41.080 --> 09:42.080
Depends on your point of view.

09:42.080 --> 09:45.080
You see, that happens to be my antelope meat they're buying.

09:45.080 --> 09:47.080
Pirates might argue with you about that.

09:47.080 --> 09:49.080
I haven't seen you boys around.

09:49.080 --> 09:50.080
Are you staking out in Virginia City?

09:50.080 --> 09:52.080
Mark Burdette's the name.

09:52.080 --> 09:54.080
Joe Cartwright, this is my brother, Horst.

09:54.080 --> 09:55.080
Pleased to meet you.

09:55.080 --> 09:56.080
Say, he's a big fella, isn't he?

09:56.080 --> 09:59.080
Boys, do you have any idea how many people are heading toward Virginia City right now?

09:59.080 --> 10:02.080
Thousands, yes, sir, thousands.

10:02.080 --> 10:05.080
And every blessed one of them with a belly he's got to fill.

10:05.080 --> 10:06.080
Gonna be a bunch of them, huh?

10:06.080 --> 10:13.080
Ever since they found out about that blue stuff being silver, which assays are better than thirty-five hundred dollars a ton, they're heading here from all over the world.

10:13.080 --> 10:15.080
Silver?

10:15.080 --> 10:19.080
All that time Comstock and those other fellows were checking it away, thinking only about gold.

10:19.080 --> 10:23.080
Gold? Virginia City's gonna be a hundred times the strike the motherlode ever was.

10:23.080 --> 10:24.080
Now, let me tell you something, boys.

10:24.080 --> 10:26.080
There's more than one way to strike it rich.

10:26.080 --> 10:30.080
Man can live without whiskey and women and clothing, even shelter.

10:30.080 --> 10:33.080
But if he doesn't eat, he dies.

10:33.080 --> 10:34.080
Hey, little Joe.

10:34.080 --> 10:35.080
What are you doing here?

10:35.080 --> 10:36.080
Bob.

10:36.080 --> 10:37.080
If I'd like you to meet Mark, what's that?

10:37.080 --> 10:38.080
He owns this place.

10:38.080 --> 10:39.080
How proud to meet you, Mr. Cartwright.

10:39.080 --> 10:40.080
Howdy.

10:40.080 --> 10:41.080
This is my brother, Adam.

10:41.080 --> 10:42.080
Adam.

10:42.080 --> 10:43.080
Howdy.

10:43.080 --> 10:44.080
You got a good thing here, haven't you?

10:44.080 --> 10:46.080
It takes a businessman to know a good business, Mr. Cartwright.

10:46.080 --> 10:47.080
Is that what you call it?

10:47.080 --> 10:49.080
I could think of another name.

10:49.080 --> 10:53.080
You boys sound as if you want to talk.

10:53.080 --> 10:56.080
Well, one thing you'll find out about me, I'm always ready to oblige.

10:56.080 --> 10:57.080
This way, gentlemen.

10:57.080 --> 10:59.080
Here we are.

10:59.080 --> 11:02.080
It's not very much, but it's the beginning.

11:02.080 --> 11:06.080
What I say is let them have their silver as long as I can sell them their meat.

11:06.080 --> 11:08.080
You're charging pretty fancy prices for that meat.

11:08.080 --> 11:10.080
It's the only meat in town, Mr. Cartwright.

11:10.080 --> 11:11.080
It cost me a lot to get it.

11:11.080 --> 11:13.080
Well, I will have cost you a lot more.

11:13.080 --> 11:16.080
Mr. You went out and butchered the meat supply of the whole Paiute nation.

11:16.080 --> 11:17.080
You're risking an Indian war.

11:17.080 --> 11:18.080
Oh, come now, friend.

11:18.080 --> 11:19.080
I have nothing against the Indians.

11:19.080 --> 11:22.080
What I always say is fair game is fair game.

11:22.080 --> 11:23.080
Hey, Pop.

11:23.080 --> 11:25.080
Why don't we sell some of our stock to Mr. Baudet here?

11:25.080 --> 11:27.080
Then the Paiutes can have the antelope to themselves again.

11:27.080 --> 11:28.080
What stock are you talking about, son?

11:28.080 --> 11:29.080
Don't you know about the Ponderosa?

11:29.080 --> 11:30.080
We've got more prime cattle.

11:30.080 --> 11:31.080
Joe.

11:33.080 --> 11:35.080
You have.

11:35.080 --> 11:38.080
Real prime beef east of the Sierras.

11:38.080 --> 11:39.080
I'll tell you what I'll do, Mr. Cartwright.

11:39.080 --> 11:41.080
I'll take all you've got.

11:41.080 --> 11:42.080
You can name your own price.

11:42.080 --> 11:46.080
If you charge $10 a pound for antelope meat, what'll you be charging for beef?

11:46.080 --> 11:47.080
All I can get.

11:47.080 --> 11:49.080
If you think that's out of line, take a look in the saloon

11:49.080 --> 11:51.080
and see what rot-gut whiskey's going for.

11:51.080 --> 11:53.080
Or a bag of flour or a pick and shovel.

11:53.080 --> 11:55.080
I just sold the last side of antelope, Mr. Baudet.

11:56.080 --> 11:57.080
We're out of business.

11:57.080 --> 11:58.080
Not yet, Thornton.

11:58.080 --> 12:01.080
These gentlemen are the Cartwrights from the Ponderosa Ranch.

12:01.080 --> 12:02.080
Prime beef cattle as much as you want.

12:02.080 --> 12:04.080
My assistant, Earl Thornton.

12:04.080 --> 12:05.080
How are you, gents?

12:05.080 --> 12:06.080
Well, do we do business?

12:06.080 --> 12:07.080
Why not, Pa?

12:07.080 --> 12:09.080
We're in the business to sell cattle.

12:09.080 --> 12:13.080
Mr. Baudet, we have our own way of doing business in the Ponderosa.

12:13.080 --> 12:16.080
We pay an honest day's wages for an honest day's work.

12:16.080 --> 12:17.080
We expect the same in return.

12:17.080 --> 12:19.080
Nothing more, nothing less.

12:19.080 --> 12:20.080
You referring to us, mister?

12:20.080 --> 12:21.080
It's all right, Thornton.

12:21.080 --> 12:22.080
Now, let's be honest, friends.

12:22.080 --> 12:23.080
I need your cattle.

12:23.080 --> 12:25.080
I'm willing to pay you the best price you'll ever get.

12:25.080 --> 12:28.080
I have a cold storage tunnel out there full of ice from the Sierras.

12:28.080 --> 12:29.080
It's the only ice in town.

12:29.080 --> 12:32.080
If you're gonna sell in Virginia City, you'll have to sell to me anyhow.

12:32.080 --> 12:33.080
I say let's get together.

12:33.080 --> 12:34.080
We'll both clean up.

12:34.080 --> 12:36.080
We ain't hurting for customers, Mr. Baudet.

12:36.080 --> 12:39.080
Any miner in town can come up to the Ponderosa and buy all the meat he needs.

12:39.080 --> 12:41.080
And we don't intend to profit from his hunger.

12:41.080 --> 12:42.080
Profit from their hunger?

12:42.080 --> 12:45.080
You think I was twisting those fellows' arms to get them in here?

12:45.080 --> 12:48.080
Every minute they can spare, they use to dig for silver.

12:48.080 --> 12:50.080
I'm doing them a service.

12:50.080 --> 12:52.080
My son is right.

12:52.080 --> 12:54.080
The Ponderosa's a business.

12:54.080 --> 12:57.080
But there's more involved here than profits.

12:57.080 --> 12:58.080
I'm sorry, Mr. Baudet.

12:58.080 --> 12:59.080
No deal.

12:59.080 --> 13:00.080
Why not?

13:00.080 --> 13:02.080
I'm offering you top dollar.

13:02.080 --> 13:04.080
And charging top dollar to people who can't afford to pay.

13:04.080 --> 13:06.080
Maybe you need seconds out of pay.

13:07.080 --> 13:08.080
Thornton!

13:08.080 --> 13:10.080
You could be foolish, mister.

13:10.080 --> 13:12.080
I told you about your temper.

13:15.080 --> 13:17.080
I'm sorry about this gentleman.

13:17.080 --> 13:19.080
But we can't let it interfere with our negotiations.

13:19.080 --> 13:21.080
Our negotiations are over.

13:21.080 --> 13:23.080
I want to warn you again.

13:23.080 --> 13:25.080
Stop slaughtering the wild herds.

13:25.080 --> 13:28.080
If you don't want a war in your hands, you follow this advice.

13:28.080 --> 13:31.080
The pirates can be unpleasant.

13:43.080 --> 13:45.080
She'll be one of them cut-writes.

13:45.080 --> 13:49.080
Thornton, when are you going to learn there's more than one way of getting what you want?

13:49.080 --> 13:50.080
Are you sure, Mr. Baudet?

13:50.080 --> 13:51.080
I'm sure.

13:51.080 --> 13:56.080
They'll sell to me before I'm through, or they'll never sell cattle to anyone else.

13:58.080 --> 14:00.080
Oh, hi there, Mr. Cartwright.

14:00.080 --> 14:02.080
What do you think of Virginia City?

14:02.080 --> 14:04.080
Sure is growing up, ain't she?

14:04.080 --> 14:05.080
Sure is, Mr. Harris.

14:05.080 --> 14:07.080
Now, this place is busier than a nest of hornets.

14:07.080 --> 14:09.080
Where you fixing to go?

14:09.080 --> 14:12.080
Oh, I got a little digging to do up Six Mile Canyon.

14:12.080 --> 14:18.080
You know, back in Canetuck, I never thought that I'd be living on a mountain of solid silver.

14:18.080 --> 14:22.080
Kind of takes a man's mind off other things, though.

14:22.080 --> 14:23.080
What about them cut-writes?

14:23.080 --> 14:25.080
There they are.

14:25.080 --> 14:28.080
Now, don't you let her take your mind off those cattle.

14:28.080 --> 14:31.080
You get some people together and come on over first thing in the morning, we'll fix you up.

14:31.080 --> 14:35.080
By golly, I'll do that first thing in the morning, and I want to thank you all.

14:35.080 --> 14:37.080
That's a real neighborly thing to do.

14:37.080 --> 14:40.080
I bet them two boys make mighty good help when it comes digging, don't they, Mr. Harris?

14:40.080 --> 14:41.080
We sure do.

14:41.080 --> 14:44.080
Yeah, well, they'll be even better when we get a little beef on their bones.

14:44.080 --> 14:48.080
We'll see you. Bye, boys.

14:48.080 --> 14:50.080
You heard what they're fixing to do.

14:50.080 --> 14:53.080
Shoot, the cut-writes are going to sell beef direct to the miners.

14:53.080 --> 14:54.080
That'll wreck us, Burdette.

14:54.080 --> 14:56.080
It could if those cattle reach Virginia City.

14:56.080 --> 14:58.080
Stop them?

14:58.080 --> 15:02.080
Let's just say I don't look with favor upon any unnecessary competition.

15:02.080 --> 15:05.080
If anyone's looking for a hornet, tell them I'm investigating the places of the bucket of blood.

15:05.080 --> 15:22.080
Right.

15:22.080 --> 15:27.080
You were just about to buy me a drink, weren't you?

15:27.080 --> 15:29.080
How did you guess?

15:29.080 --> 15:32.080
I suppose I just have a knack for certain things.

15:32.080 --> 15:36.080
Uh-huh. I'm sure you have.

15:36.080 --> 15:41.080
Oh, um, isn't there some kind of a rule about women frequenting saloons?

15:41.080 --> 15:45.080
Who didn't you know? This is Virginia City. Anything goes.

15:45.080 --> 15:51.080
Exactly my sentiments. After you.

15:51.080 --> 15:56.080
Well, it isn't exactly the Palace Hotel in San Francisco, but it will have to do.

15:56.080 --> 16:00.080
The name's Gloria DeLacy, and it's all right. I've been in here before.

16:00.080 --> 16:03.080
Then you'll know what kind of whiskey to order.

16:03.080 --> 16:05.080
It's all one kind. Rock that.

16:05.080 --> 16:06.080
Now, let's see if you're right.

16:06.080 --> 16:09.080
A bartender, a bottle of your very finest.

16:09.080 --> 16:13.080
Why is it that a new mining camp always has the worst kind of whiskey?

16:13.080 --> 16:15.080
The worst kind of women?

16:15.080 --> 16:19.080
That wasn't what I was thinking.

16:19.080 --> 16:20.080
What were you thinking?

16:20.080 --> 16:25.080
That you are the only really beautiful thing I've seen in Virginia City.

16:25.080 --> 16:28.080
Why haven't I seen you before?

16:28.080 --> 16:30.080
Just got in town a few days ago.

16:30.080 --> 16:34.080
Well, let's celebrate.

16:34.080 --> 16:40.080
Thank you.

16:40.080 --> 16:41.080
What's your name?

16:41.080 --> 16:44.080
Burdett. Mark Burdett.

16:44.080 --> 16:47.080
To glory of the Comstock load.

16:47.080 --> 16:50.080
To the Comstock load.

16:50.080 --> 16:53.080
They say it'll be the biggest and richest strike in history.

16:53.080 --> 16:58.080
Bonanza. A real bonanza. And I'm gonna get my share of it.

16:58.080 --> 17:01.080
You're not exactly dressed for the part.

17:01.080 --> 17:04.080
Oh, you don't think I mean to dig for it like those fellows over there?

17:04.080 --> 17:07.080
There's more than one way of panning for silver.

17:07.080 --> 17:10.080
Yeah, I know.

17:10.080 --> 17:13.080
I didn't mean it that way.

17:13.080 --> 17:15.080
Why are you here?

17:15.080 --> 17:18.080
The excitement of a new camp.

17:18.080 --> 17:20.080
I don't know.

17:20.080 --> 17:23.080
Maybe the hope that this one will be it.

17:23.080 --> 17:25.080
Anyway, there's nothing left in California.

17:25.080 --> 17:27.080
This is gonna be the biggest thing that ever happened.

17:27.080 --> 17:29.080
Make California look sick. I can feel it.

17:29.080 --> 17:33.080
And this time, I mean to get my share of it.

17:33.080 --> 17:35.080
How come you never made it in California?

17:35.080 --> 17:38.080
Smart man like you.

17:38.080 --> 17:42.080
Maybe I wasn't smart enough.

17:42.080 --> 17:44.080
Come to think of it, I could ask you the same question, couldn't I?

17:44.080 --> 17:46.080
Don't.

17:46.080 --> 17:47.080
To the future.

17:47.080 --> 17:50.080
When we both have what we want, you care to drink to it?

17:50.080 --> 17:54.080
As long as you're buying the drinks, Mr. Baudet, I'll drink to anything.

17:54.080 --> 17:57.080
I'm gonna be rich. The richest man in town.

17:57.080 --> 18:00.080
He's wishing you luck.

18:00.080 --> 18:09.080
What I mean to say is that from now on, I don't want anyone else buying you drinks.

18:09.080 --> 18:12.080
You mean you want to take care of everything?

18:12.080 --> 18:27.080
I'm gonna take care of everything.

18:27.080 --> 18:29.080
We're eating steak tonight.

18:29.080 --> 18:54.080
Get ready.

18:54.080 --> 19:05.080
Remember, I'll take care of the wounded if we left alive.

19:05.080 --> 19:18.080
Get him.

19:18.080 --> 19:34.080
Don't shoot!

19:34.080 --> 19:49.080
Your kids. What are we gonna tell it?

19:49.080 --> 19:54.080
It's all over town, Thorn. Fever's running high against the Indians.

19:54.080 --> 19:56.080
Did you have to kill that way?

19:56.080 --> 19:58.080
Them cattle didn't get to Virginia City, did they?

19:58.080 --> 20:01.080
All right, they didn't, but you could have stopped short of murder.

20:01.080 --> 20:03.080
You know any other way, Mr. Baudet?

20:03.080 --> 20:06.080
The Cartwrights would have come around and up the price until they had no choice.

20:06.080 --> 20:11.080
Someday you're gonna learn it takes more than money to make a real killing.

20:11.080 --> 20:15.080
Thorn, you're a monster.

20:15.080 --> 20:18.080
I never should have taken up with you again.

20:18.080 --> 20:20.080
You need me, Baudet.

20:20.080 --> 20:24.080
Remember we have a murder charge hanging over us back in St. Louis?

20:24.080 --> 20:37.080
Would you forget about that prison guard that killed you? You could get to be a free man again.

20:37.080 --> 20:43.080
Here you are. Three kings.

20:43.080 --> 20:46.080
All right, boys, party's over. We got some more work to do.

20:46.080 --> 20:47.080
I thought we'd done enough, Thorn.

20:47.080 --> 20:50.080
Job's only half done. There's still the other half.

20:50.080 --> 20:51.080
Yeah, what's that?

20:51.080 --> 20:54.080
There's plenty of riled up against the Indians for killing them miners.

20:54.080 --> 20:56.080
Well, they're getting the posse together to go after them.

20:56.080 --> 20:59.080
Yeah, I know. That's why we gotta get the Indians stood up against the miners.

20:59.080 --> 21:01.080
That way we put the Cartwrights' plum in the middle.

21:01.080 --> 21:02.080
And what's on your mind?

21:02.080 --> 21:04.080
Killing the St. Pius.

21:04.080 --> 21:06.080
For having massacred those poor, hardworking miners.

21:06.080 --> 21:08.080
Why don't we let the posse go after them?

21:08.080 --> 21:11.080
Because the posse might stop long enough to ask questions I don't like questions.

21:11.080 --> 21:14.080
You mean like, who really killed those miners?

21:14.080 --> 21:16.080
What's the idea?

21:16.080 --> 21:18.080
I told you I don't like questions.

21:18.080 --> 21:20.080
You really are smart, aren't you, Thorn?

21:20.080 --> 21:23.080
Smart enough to know a dead man can't talk, even to a posse.

21:25.080 --> 21:27.080
What's the name of that Indian that works for the Cartwrights?

21:28.080 --> 21:29.080
Did you hear me?

21:29.080 --> 21:30.080
Duqua.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.080
Duqua.

21:32.080 --> 21:34.080
All right, boys, let's get moving.

21:34.080 --> 21:36.080
We gotta get to him before somebody else does.

21:36.080 --> 21:54.080
Get your hands up.

22:06.080 --> 22:24.080
It was the diggers from Sun Mountain.

22:24.080 --> 22:28.080
Some of my people saw them as they drove the cattle toward the waters.

22:28.080 --> 22:30.080
Are you sure, Widermacher?

22:30.080 --> 22:32.080
The Paiute does not lie.

22:32.080 --> 22:35.080
The diggers killed the deer and the antelope.

22:35.080 --> 22:38.080
They cut down the pinyon tree, and the Paiute has no bread.

22:38.080 --> 22:41.080
And now he cuts down my young men.

22:41.080 --> 22:43.080
It's like California all over again.

22:43.080 --> 22:46.080
Whatever they touch, they kill.

22:46.080 --> 22:48.080
How would anybody want to kill Duqua?

22:48.080 --> 22:52.080
Vengeance, some strange notion of vengeance.

22:52.080 --> 22:54.080
It just don't make sense, Pa.

22:54.080 --> 22:56.080
Them miners is all killed with bullets.

22:56.080 --> 22:58.080
The Paiutes use arrows.

22:58.080 --> 23:01.080
I guess he didn't have much chance to tell them that.

23:01.080 --> 23:05.080
What will my young men say when I tell them of their brother's murder?

23:05.080 --> 23:08.080
You must keep them in hand, Widermacher.

23:08.080 --> 23:11.080
Let the Ponderosa find the men who did this.

23:11.080 --> 23:15.080
I am an old man leading a thousand stallions.

23:15.080 --> 23:18.080
Today I can stop my young braves.

23:18.080 --> 23:21.080
I do not know if I can tomorrow.

23:21.080 --> 23:41.080
We will return for Duqua.

23:41.080 --> 23:43.080
Let's find out who did this.

23:43.080 --> 23:44.080
I know who.

23:44.080 --> 23:45.080
Who?

23:45.080 --> 23:47.080
Mark Burdett.

23:47.080 --> 23:49.080
Wait a minute, Adam. Don't you think you're pushing this a little bit?

23:49.080 --> 23:52.080
I know you don't like Burdett, but you heard Widermacher say some miners did this.

23:52.080 --> 23:53.080
Burdett's no miner.

23:53.080 --> 23:57.080
At the moment, he's the only man who stands to make a profit by starting trouble between the ranchers and the miners.

23:57.080 --> 23:58.080
Not to mention the Indians.

23:58.080 --> 24:00.080
Pa, we've got nothing to go on.

24:00.080 --> 24:04.080
If we listen to Adam, we may ride into Virginia City and hang an innocent man.

24:04.080 --> 24:06.080
Well, he has a point there, Adam.

24:06.080 --> 24:07.080
We have no proof.

24:07.080 --> 24:09.080
You've met Burdett. How much proof do you need?

24:09.080 --> 24:11.080
Enough to know that we've got the right man.

24:11.080 --> 24:15.080
Why don't you let me go into Virginia City and snoop around, see what I can pick up?

24:15.080 --> 24:16.080
Alone?

24:16.080 --> 24:18.080
Sure. If we all go in together, everyone will see us.

24:18.080 --> 24:20.080
If I go in by myself, I won't be noticed.

24:20.080 --> 24:22.080
Might not be a bad idea, Pa.

24:22.080 --> 24:24.080
Well, maybe.

24:24.080 --> 24:26.080
Now, you take care of yourself, little Joe.

24:26.080 --> 24:29.080
Don't let Burdett sell you half interest in his business.

24:29.080 --> 24:31.080
Might not be a bad investment.

24:31.080 --> 24:35.080
Little Joe, maybe I want to ride in with you, huh?

24:35.080 --> 24:39.080
Of course, I'd be less noticed if I rode down the main street with a couple of wild steers.

24:39.080 --> 25:04.080
Don't worry, I'll take care of myself.

25:04.080 --> 25:06.080
It's your cart register again, alone.

25:06.080 --> 25:09.080
You're taking quite a chance, isn't he, riding into Virginia City alone?

25:09.080 --> 25:12.080
Especially if word gets around that the cartwright is assigned with the Paiutes.

25:12.080 --> 25:14.080
What do you think would happen to him if it did?

25:14.080 --> 25:16.080
I don't know. There's almost anything.

25:16.080 --> 25:17.080
I wouldn't want him hurt bad.

25:17.080 --> 25:20.080
I have a feeling that Joe Cartwright and I are going to be friends.

25:20.080 --> 25:29.080
Yeah, good friends.

25:29.080 --> 25:33.080
Hey, kid.

25:33.080 --> 25:35.080
You talking to me, mister?

25:35.080 --> 25:56.080
Yeah, I'm talking to you, you muttering little skunk.

25:56.080 --> 26:09.080
Get out of here.

26:09.080 --> 26:10.080
One of them cartwrights.

26:10.080 --> 26:12.080
Messed with those murdering thieving Paiutes.

26:12.080 --> 26:13.080
Paiutes?

26:13.080 --> 26:15.080
Somebody get a rope.

26:15.080 --> 26:17.080
No, don't do it. He can do it.

26:17.080 --> 26:19.080
He's going to shoot him.

26:19.080 --> 26:21.080
Let him go.

26:21.080 --> 26:27.080
What is all this?

26:27.080 --> 26:29.080
We're going to hang ourselves in engine, Lover.

26:29.080 --> 26:31.080
Nobody's going to hang this boy.

26:31.080 --> 26:33.080
We got three men dead over those Paiutes.

26:33.080 --> 26:37.080
Don't say Joe Cartwright hears any part of it.

26:37.080 --> 26:38.080
Who started this, you?

26:38.080 --> 26:40.080
Yeah, so what?

26:40.080 --> 26:44.080
It's on your fire. I don't want to see you around my place anymore.

26:44.080 --> 26:47.080
Here you go. Take him into my office.

26:47.080 --> 26:50.080
Open up. Let him through.

26:50.080 --> 26:53.080
What is this?

26:53.080 --> 27:08.080
Anybody want to argue about anything?

27:08.080 --> 27:10.080
Did I hurt you?

27:10.080 --> 27:13.080
I don't think you could hurt me, ma'am.

27:13.080 --> 27:16.080
I don't understand. Those miners out in the street, they wanted to hang me. Why?

27:16.080 --> 27:18.080
You don't know?

27:18.080 --> 27:20.080
Well, the miners sent two groups out to buy cattle.

27:20.080 --> 27:22.080
One of them went down to your place.

27:22.080 --> 27:24.080
That's right. We sold them about half dozen a head.

27:24.080 --> 27:26.080
The other one from Gold Hill down toward Carson.

27:26.080 --> 27:28.080
They found both groups murdered. Cattle were gone.

27:28.080 --> 27:30.080
Well, it makes me think it was the Paiutes.

27:30.080 --> 27:32.080
One of the miners, a man named Harris, managed to stay alive.

27:32.080 --> 27:37.080
He recognized one of the Indians, a fellow called Tukwa.

27:37.080 --> 27:39.080
That's a lie.

27:39.080 --> 27:41.080
Easy, Joe. He said it, not me.

27:41.080 --> 27:44.080
Anyway, that's why this Tukwa is dead. They would have hung him anyway.

27:44.080 --> 27:48.080
Tukwa's not that kind of a man. He'd never take a part in anything like this.

27:48.080 --> 27:50.080
Mr. Biddett, you help me out there in the street.

27:50.080 --> 27:52.080
I can't think of us as friends.

27:52.080 --> 27:54.080
You can believe me about Tukwa.

27:54.080 --> 27:57.080
No, I don't want to believe it. Drop it.

27:57.080 --> 27:59.080
Drop it. What do you mean?

27:59.080 --> 28:01.080
Well, I said, it's all over now. This Indian, whatever his name was...

28:01.080 --> 28:03.080
His name was Tukwa.

28:03.080 --> 28:05.080
All right, that's Tukwa. Anyway, he's dead now, and he deserved to die.

28:05.080 --> 28:07.080
He took part in that massacre.

28:07.080 --> 28:09.080
But he didn't, Mr. Biddett. Not Tukwa. I know.

28:09.080 --> 28:11.080
How do you know?

28:11.080 --> 28:13.080
You fool. How do you know?

28:13.080 --> 28:15.080
I told you, he was identified.

28:15.080 --> 28:17.080
Yeah, that's right. You told me.

28:17.080 --> 28:19.080
Thanks for the help.

28:22.080 --> 28:24.080
I'll buy you a drink someday, ma'am.

28:24.080 --> 28:26.080
You know where to find me.

28:26.080 --> 28:28.080
I'll find you.

28:34.080 --> 28:36.080
You were pretty nice to that kid.

28:36.080 --> 28:38.080
It's my job.

28:38.080 --> 28:40.080
You're a good kid.

28:40.080 --> 28:42.080
It's my job. Being nice to people.

28:42.080 --> 28:45.080
Paying customers, you mean. He wasn't a paying customer.

28:45.080 --> 28:47.080
And you are, aren't you, Mr. Biddett?

28:47.080 --> 28:49.080
You bought me three drinks.

28:49.080 --> 28:51.080
Or was it four?

28:51.080 --> 28:53.080
That didn't count. Look, what's bothering you?

28:53.080 --> 28:55.080
You, if you want to know.

28:55.080 --> 28:57.080
What about me?

28:57.080 --> 28:59.080
I don't want you fooling around with anyone else, do you hear?

28:59.080 --> 29:01.080
I told you I'm going to be the biggest man in this town.

29:01.080 --> 29:08.080
Then God have mercy on this town.

29:14.080 --> 29:16.080
I'm sorry, Gloria. I didn't mean that.

29:18.080 --> 29:20.080
I'm glad you did it.

29:20.080 --> 29:23.080
Because now I don't owe you a thing for those three drinks.

29:23.080 --> 29:25.080
What's bothering you?

29:25.080 --> 29:27.080
You act as though I've done something wrong. What have I done?

29:27.080 --> 29:29.080
I'm not sure.

29:29.080 --> 29:31.080
But if it's what I'm thinking.

29:31.080 --> 29:33.080
What are you thinking?

29:33.080 --> 29:36.080
That maybe, just maybe, it was you who ordered that massacre.

29:36.080 --> 29:39.080
No, that isn't true. You heard about Harris identifying Tukwa.

29:39.080 --> 29:41.080
I heard you identify him, Mr. Biddett.

29:41.080 --> 29:43.080
I didn't hear anything else.

29:43.080 --> 30:10.080
I didn't hear Mr. Harris say anything.

30:10.080 --> 30:12.080
Well, there he is now.

30:12.080 --> 30:14.080
About time.

30:14.080 --> 30:16.080
Where have you been? We were worried about you.

30:16.080 --> 30:18.080
Sit down and eat and tell us what you found out.

30:23.080 --> 30:25.080
Little Joe, what did he do to you, boy?

30:25.080 --> 30:27.080
What happened to your face?

30:27.080 --> 30:29.080
Forget it.

30:29.080 --> 30:31.080
Who did it? Now hold still a minute. Now who did it?

30:31.080 --> 30:33.080
Some miners in Virginia City. I said forget it.

30:33.080 --> 30:35.080
They beat you like this?

30:35.080 --> 30:37.080
They'd have hanged me if Mark Biddett hadn't stopped them.

30:37.080 --> 30:39.080
Hanged you? For what?

30:39.080 --> 30:41.080
Being a friend of the Paiutes.

30:41.080 --> 30:43.080
I'm talking about the man who staged that massacre.

30:43.080 --> 30:45.080
That's a lie.

30:45.080 --> 30:47.080
Yeah, that's what I tried to tell him. But what good it did me.

30:47.080 --> 30:49.080
Who's the one who identified Tukwa?

30:49.080 --> 30:51.080
The one that came out of it alive. That fellow named Harris.

30:51.080 --> 30:53.080
Adam, what are you up to?

30:53.080 --> 30:55.080
I'm gonna have a little talk with our friend Harris.

30:55.080 --> 30:57.080
No, wait. Don't run in there alone. We'll go with you.

31:03.080 --> 31:05.080
Where have you been?

31:05.080 --> 31:07.080
Just standing away.

31:07.080 --> 31:09.080
After all, you fired me.

31:09.080 --> 31:11.080
I'm sorry.

31:13.080 --> 31:15.080
You look worried, Biddett.

31:15.080 --> 31:17.080
Don't remember seeing you look that way before.

31:17.080 --> 31:19.080
You're saying things. There isn't anything I can't handle.

31:19.080 --> 31:21.080
Sure, sure.

31:21.080 --> 31:23.080
Like that girl I seen walk out of here.

31:23.080 --> 31:25.080
That one named Glory.

31:25.080 --> 31:27.080
Why do you mention her?

31:27.080 --> 31:29.080
She doesn't have anything to do with it.

31:29.080 --> 31:31.080
She don't, huh?

31:31.080 --> 31:33.080
Well, I'm real glad to hear that.

31:33.080 --> 31:35.080
Because I just seen her going after the Harris place.

31:35.080 --> 31:37.080
The Harris place?

31:37.080 --> 31:39.080
The Harris place tells of the truth.

31:39.080 --> 31:41.080
I thought you and me came to Virginia City to strike it rich.

31:41.080 --> 31:43.080
Now stretch a rope.

31:55.080 --> 31:57.080
Well, hello, boys.

31:57.080 --> 31:59.080
Hello, ma'am.

31:59.080 --> 32:01.080
You're pretty busy, aren't you?

32:01.080 --> 32:03.080
We are. We're standing for gold, ma'am.

32:03.080 --> 32:05.080
Gold? Does anybody ever find it?

32:05.080 --> 32:07.080
You want anything here?

32:07.080 --> 32:09.080
You're Mrs. Harris, aren't you?

32:09.080 --> 32:11.080
Yes, I'm Mrs. Harris.

32:11.080 --> 32:13.080
I'm pleased to know you, ma'am.

32:13.080 --> 32:15.080
I'm glad...

32:15.080 --> 32:17.080
I know who you are.

32:17.080 --> 32:19.080
What do you want here?

32:19.080 --> 32:21.080
I'd like to see your husband.

32:21.080 --> 32:23.080
My husband?

32:23.080 --> 32:25.080
You know my husband?

32:25.080 --> 32:27.080
No.

32:27.080 --> 32:39.080
But I must talk with him. It's very important.

32:39.080 --> 32:41.080
How is he?

32:41.080 --> 32:47.080
Since he was hurt out there, he does nothing but stare at the ceiling.

32:47.080 --> 32:57.080
Sometimes he talks, but mostly he just stares.

32:57.080 --> 33:01.080
Carl?

33:01.080 --> 33:05.080
There's somebody here who wants to talk to you.

33:05.080 --> 33:09.080
A woman.

33:09.080 --> 33:12.080
Mr. Harris.

33:12.080 --> 33:18.080
Mr. Harris, I've got to know about that Indian attack.

33:18.080 --> 33:21.080
What do you want to know?

33:21.080 --> 33:24.080
That Indian. The one that rode for the Cartwrights.

33:24.080 --> 33:27.080
The one they called Tukwa.

33:27.080 --> 33:32.080
Did you see him during the attack?

33:32.080 --> 33:37.080
I don't even know who he is.

33:37.080 --> 33:41.080
Then you couldn't have identified him, could you?

33:41.080 --> 33:49.080
I couldn't identify anybody.

33:49.080 --> 33:52.080
Thank you, Mr. Harris.

33:52.080 --> 33:57.080
Thank you very much.

33:57.080 --> 33:59.080
Thank you, ma'am.

33:59.080 --> 34:08.080
I sure hope your luck changes for the better soon.

34:08.080 --> 34:11.080
Goodbye, boys. I sure hope you find that gold.

34:11.080 --> 34:15.080
We will. We just got to keep on digging, though.

34:15.080 --> 34:17.080
She's pretty.

34:17.080 --> 34:19.080
Hey, Mike, keep digging.

34:19.080 --> 34:25.080
All right.

34:25.080 --> 34:26.080
What are they doing to her?

34:26.080 --> 34:28.080
I don't know.

34:28.080 --> 34:33.080
We won't hurt you, Gloria, but you better go with us.

34:33.080 --> 34:34.080
Don't you ever hit her again.

34:34.080 --> 34:38.080
Who's going to stop me, bird dick? You?

34:38.080 --> 34:39.080
They're hurting her.

34:39.080 --> 34:41.080
Ma!

34:41.080 --> 34:43.080
Mike, why are you doing this?

34:43.080 --> 34:44.080
What is it, Michael?

34:44.080 --> 34:45.080
They're hurting her.

34:45.080 --> 34:46.080
Who?

34:46.080 --> 34:57.080
The lady that just left the house.

34:57.080 --> 34:59.080
Carl, they've taken that girl away.

34:59.080 --> 35:01.080
I got to get to town, get help.

35:01.080 --> 35:05.080
It was just a bare rock farm.

35:05.080 --> 35:16.080
Man had to take a chance with his wife, his boys.

35:16.080 --> 35:24.080
You boys stay here in case your pa needs something.

35:24.080 --> 35:27.080
Harris, we'd like to have a talk with your husband.

35:27.080 --> 35:28.080
The girl. They've taken the girl.

35:28.080 --> 35:31.080
The girl?

35:31.080 --> 35:32.080
What girl?

35:32.080 --> 35:34.080
I don't know her name. She works in the saloon.

35:34.080 --> 35:35.080
You mean Gloria?

35:35.080 --> 35:37.080
You got to help. They'll kill her.

35:37.080 --> 35:40.080
Harris, just try to calm yourself and tell us what happened.

35:40.080 --> 35:43.080
It was that man named Thorn. They were beating her.

35:43.080 --> 35:45.080
They? Who? Who was with Thorn?

35:45.080 --> 35:47.080
The man he works for, the one that wears the fancy clothes.

35:47.080 --> 35:49.080
Two men beating up on a girl?

35:49.080 --> 35:53.080
They rode out of town. Thorn had the girl.

35:53.080 --> 35:55.080
Adam, I was wrong about him. I'm sorry.

35:55.080 --> 35:57.080
Forget it, younger brother.

35:57.080 --> 35:58.080
What do we do about the girl?

35:58.080 --> 36:01.080
We find her. Don't we, Pa?

36:01.080 --> 36:21.080
Yeah, we find her. Come on.

36:21.080 --> 36:24.080
Think I can run away out here?

36:24.080 --> 36:25.080
Thanks.

36:25.080 --> 36:27.080
Where's that line shack you were talking about, Thorn?

36:27.080 --> 36:29.080
Should be just over that hill.

36:29.080 --> 36:33.080
Yeah.

36:33.080 --> 36:37.080
Oh. Oh.

36:37.080 --> 36:39.080
I sure would like to get my hands on that thorn.

36:39.080 --> 36:41.080
You'll get your chance as soon as we find the girl.

36:41.080 --> 36:43.080
Toss, you think he can tell which way they're heading?

36:43.080 --> 36:46.080
Pa, if I read the signs right,

36:46.080 --> 36:49.080
it looks to me like they're trying to make the other side of Devil's Gate.

36:49.080 --> 36:50.080
You think so?

36:50.080 --> 36:54.080
Just the hottest, driest, drippest desert in Nevada territory.

36:54.080 --> 37:02.080
All right, let's go.

37:02.080 --> 37:04.080
Now, this is Devil's Gate, isn't it, Thorn?

37:04.080 --> 37:05.080
Yeah, it sure is.

37:05.080 --> 37:06.080
Where's the shack?

37:06.080 --> 37:08.080
Just over the ridge.

37:08.080 --> 37:10.080
You sure?

37:10.080 --> 37:15.080
It wouldn't make much difference if I wasn't, would it, Mr. Burdett?

37:15.080 --> 37:17.080
Why don't you kill him, Burdett?

37:17.080 --> 37:19.080
Where did you get that idea?

37:19.080 --> 37:22.080
I thought you were the biggest man in Virginia City.

37:22.080 --> 37:27.080
All right, prove it. Kill him.

37:27.080 --> 37:43.080
Think you can do it, Mr. Burdett?

37:43.080 --> 37:45.080
You're right, Hoss. They're headed for Devil's Gate.

37:45.080 --> 37:46.080
Wait a minute, little girl.

37:46.080 --> 37:48.080
Can't be too far ahead with one horse riding double.

37:48.080 --> 37:51.080
Adam, you little joke, cut around that hill.

37:51.080 --> 37:53.080
Hoss and I will plot the gap on this end.

37:53.080 --> 37:54.080
Sounds good, Pa.

37:54.080 --> 38:15.080
Come on.

38:15.080 --> 38:17.080
You were lying, Thorn. I should have known it.

38:17.080 --> 38:19.080
Now, why would I do a thing like that, huh?

38:19.080 --> 38:20.080
Come on.

38:20.080 --> 38:22.080
There isn't anything there.

38:22.080 --> 38:30.080
Well, there's plenty of space. Long, dry, hot space.

38:30.080 --> 38:32.080
Want a drink, miss?

38:32.080 --> 38:34.080
Of course, they handle that fancy whiskey like you used to have them.

38:34.080 --> 38:36.080
I don't want anything from you.

38:36.080 --> 38:41.080
Good, because that's exactly what you're going to get.

38:41.080 --> 38:45.080
Is that what you were planning, Thorn, to turn a loose in that desert without water?

38:45.080 --> 38:48.080
She's the only thing between you and me making a real killing partner.

38:48.080 --> 38:51.080
I want to kill you, Thorn.

38:51.080 --> 38:59.080
And just how do you plan to do that, Mr. Burditt?

38:59.080 --> 39:16.080
Hey, come on.

39:16.080 --> 39:27.080
Sounds like Adam and Little Joe found them.

39:27.080 --> 39:30.080
You've got a gun, aren't you, Eustace?

39:30.080 --> 39:33.080
You look worried, Thorn. I don't remember you looking that way before.

39:33.080 --> 39:35.080
They'll kill you, you fool. You want to get killed?

39:35.080 --> 39:47.080
Get her!

39:47.080 --> 39:50.080
She got away.

39:50.080 --> 39:58.080
Oh, she doesn't.

39:58.080 --> 40:02.080
Use that gun.

40:02.080 --> 40:03.080
Use that gun, Burditt!

40:03.080 --> 40:06.080
You moved on me all along, didn't you?

40:06.080 --> 40:08.080
I didn't fool you for a minute.

40:08.080 --> 40:10.080
Not very many men fool you, Mark.

40:10.080 --> 40:14.080
I didn't either. That's what's important to me.

40:14.080 --> 40:18.080
You saw what a fake I was right from the start.

40:18.080 --> 40:20.080
Not a fake.

40:20.080 --> 40:23.080
Just a man reaching for the moon.

40:23.080 --> 40:25.080
Or anything else a million miles away.

40:25.080 --> 40:28.080
A million miles.

40:28.080 --> 40:31.080
A million dollars.

40:31.080 --> 40:34.080
Same difference, is it?

40:34.080 --> 40:46.080
You coward, you fancy-pants coward.

40:46.080 --> 40:50.080
He ain't good enough to worry about. Let him die.

40:50.080 --> 40:52.080
I said let him die.

40:52.080 --> 40:56.080
Let me go.

40:56.080 --> 41:08.080
Come any nearer, I'll shoot her in the back.

41:08.080 --> 41:09.080
Then shoot.

41:09.080 --> 41:11.080
Because Thorn can still kill the girl.

41:11.080 --> 41:21.080
Now you clear out of here. Clear out of here!

41:21.080 --> 41:46.080
Clear out of here!

41:46.080 --> 42:02.080
Boss, Boss!

42:02.080 --> 42:04.080
Boss, you all right?

42:04.080 --> 42:05.080
Yeah, man.

42:05.080 --> 42:11.080
Oh, he said he had a hard head, Pa.

42:11.080 --> 42:14.080
He's dead.

42:14.080 --> 42:17.080
He's dead, isn't he?

42:17.080 --> 42:22.080
Came here to strike it rich, find a bonanza, now he's dead.

42:22.080 --> 42:25.080
He found it.

42:25.080 --> 42:28.080
He found his bonanza.

42:28.080 --> 42:32.080
He found it just as he died.

42:32.080 --> 42:37.080
And that's better than never finding it at all, isn't it?

42:37.080 --> 42:39.080
Yes, Glory, it's better.

42:39.080 --> 42:47.080
Much better.

42:47.080 --> 42:52.080
One place or another, there'll always be a mark for debt.

42:52.080 --> 42:58.080
And for everyone like him who makes it, a thousand will fail.

42:58.080 --> 43:09.080
But then, what a thousand to one odds for a man who looks up into the sky and sees a bonanza.

43:28.080 --> 43:40.080
Up next, a show so funny even the cast can't get through it without cracking up.

43:40.080 --> 43:44.080
It's Carol Burnett and Friends, the best of the Carol Burnett Show.

43:44.080 --> 44:02.080
And it's coming up next on...

